  "name": "Inbound email to Slack (no mail server) — Webhook Relay",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📧→💬 Inbound email to Slack — no mail server\n\n**Who's it for**\nTeams that want new email (support requests, alerts, form replies) to land in a **Slack** channel — without running or exposing a mail server, and without exposing n8n to the internet.\n\n**What it does**\n[Webhook Relay](https://webhookrelay.com) gives you a real inbound email address, parses each message to JSON, and streams it to n8n over an **outbound WebSocket**. This workflow posts a tidy summary to Slack.\n\n**How it works**\n1. **Email Trigger** receives the parsed message over the socket.\n2. **Parse email** pulls out from / subject / text.\n3. **Post to Slack** sends it to your channel.\n\n**Setup (2 min)**\n1. Install `n8n-nodes-webhookrelay` (**Settings → Community Nodes → Install**).\n2. Add a **Webhook Relay API** credential — key from [my.webhookrelay.com/tokens](https://my.webhookrelay.com/tokens).\n3. Open the trigger's **Email Address** field to load your inbound address. (Optional) set **Allowed Senders** to lock it down.\n4. Connect your **Slack** credential and pick a channel on the Slack node. **Activate**, then email the address.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "cc000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
